# Where the Runs backend lives. Copy this file to `.env.local` and set your
# real value there (`.env.local` is git-ignored; this example is committed).
#
# Expo inlines any EXPO_PUBLIC_* var into the app bundle at build time, so this
# is NOT a secret — do not put tokens/passwords in EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars.
#
# RELEASE builds (anything distributed to the group) MUST use the public
# https:// tunnel URL — see "Release Gates" in runs-v1-spec.md. The realtime
# client derives wss:// from it automatically. Cleartext http is no longer
# permitted in release builds (usesCleartextTraffic was removed), so a release
# APK pointed at a plain http:// URL will refuse to connect — by design.
#
#   Release / production:           https://runs.<your-domain>
#
# DEV builds may still point at the tailnet over plain http — Android debug
# builds allow cleartext (React Native's debug manifest), so `expo run:android`
# keeps working against the tailnet. iOS dev builds have no such exception:
# point iOS dev at the https tunnel URL (or add a temporary local ATS override
# you never commit).
#
#   Same machine (Expo web):        http://localhost:4000
#   Physical device, same LAN:      http://<your-lan-ip>:4000
#   Over Tailscale (device + NAS):  http://<tailscale-ip-or-magicdns>:4000
#   Android emulator -> host:       http://10.0.2.2:4000
EXPO_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:4000
